# Build context exclusions for the app/worker Dockerfiles, built with src/docforge/ as their
# context (see app/Dockerfile's and worker/Dockerfile's own "Build note" headers, and
# compose/overlays/compose.dev.yml's `build.context: ../../src/docforge`). Anything matched here is
# NEVER sent to the daemon. Note this is a SEPARATE file from ../.dockerignore (which only
# covers the sibling `src` context used by mcp/bge_server/paddle_server) — Docker only reads
# .dockerignore from the build context root, and app/worker's context root is this directory,
# not its parent.

# ── Local Python virtualenv — host-side `uv sync` state, never needed in the image (the
#    Dockerfile builds its OWN venv via `uv sync` in the py-build stage) and would otherwise
#    ship ~400 MB of host-built, host-arch wheels into every build. ──
**/.venv
**/venv

# ── Frontend dev artefacts — the app image builds its own dist/ in the ui-build stage; a
#    host-side node_modules stub or stale dist/ (from local `npm run dev`/`npm run build`)
#    must never leak in. node_modules can also contain symlinks BuildKit rejects. ──
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.vite

# ── Python build/runtime/test artefacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage

# ── Editor / OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# ── Logs / local data ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/logs
**/*.log
